From 07e9d62aca74cd496b602c1a1b36d194e40bf15d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 03:11:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] powerinfer: POWERINFER_NO_BUFFERING=1 -- the Windows
 counterpart of the O_DIRECT Linux already uses

This same file already opens the bundle with O_RDONLY | O_DIRECT on POSIX
(iou.cpp, the Linux branch). The Windows port was brought up buffered:
FILE_FLAG_RANDOM_ACCESS, plus FILE_FLAG_OVERLAPPED in IOCP mode, and nothing
that bypasses the system file cache. So on Windows every bundle read lands in
the cache.

That is not a cosmetic difference on this box. Visible RAM is ~15.7 GB and the
SmallThinker-21B bundle is 10.28 GB, so the cache absorbs exactly what an I/O A/B
is trying to measure. Measured consequence, from this lane's own run: the
POWERINFER_IOCP arms drifted upward run-over-run as the cache warmed (iocp-on
3.63 -> 4.73 -> 5.17 across replicates) while the synchronous arm did not
(3.98 -> 4.12 -> 3.35), and the two never separated -- ranges 3.25-5.37 against
2.80-4.16. That is why the options registry has carried POWERINFER_IOCP as
"Direction UNRESOLVED" and why an earlier A/B was written off as noise.

WHY THIS COULD NOT HAVE BEEN ADDED BEFORE. NO_BUFFERING requires the file offset,
the transfer length AND the destination buffer to be sector-aligned. ExpertCache
already allocated buffers via az::aligned_alloc(io_alignment, ...), but until the
padded-stride change (a3d5215ff) it issued reads of the UNPADDED matrix length at
unpadded offsets. Those reads would have failed with ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER for
any model whose matrix was not already 4096-aligned. The stride fix was the
prerequisite, not a separate cleanup.

Default OFF, deliberately. This is a measurement instrument first: the buffered
and unbuffered paths must be A/B-able on the same binary, and defaulting it on
would silently change the meaning of every streaming number recorded so far.

Verified on the real binary before this commit: both nobuf arms loaded the bundle
("PowerInfer: loading expert bundle from" present), produced timings, and logged
no ReadFile or INVALID_PARAMETER failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 powerinfer/moe_sparse_pipeline/iou.cpp | 26 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/powerinfer/moe_sparse_pipeline/iou.cpp b/powerinfer/moe_sparse_pipeline/iou.cpp
index cbf5f62db..0ca05bb61 100644
--- a/powerinfer/moe_sparse_pipeline/iou.cpp
+++ b/powerinfer/moe_sparse_pipeline/iou.cpp
@@ -39,10 +39,34 @@ IOUring::IOUring(const std::string &path, size_t queue_depth) :
 
     // FILE_FLAG_OVERLAPPED only in IOCP mode: the synchronous path needs a
     // blocking handle so ReadFile completes in place, exactly as pre-M2b.
-    const DWORD create_flags = iocp_enabled()
+    DWORD create_flags = iocp_enabled()
         ? (FILE_FLAG_RANDOM_ACCESS | FILE_FLAG_OVERLAPPED)
         : FILE_FLAG_RANDOM_ACCESS;
 
+    // POWERINFER_NO_BUFFERING=1 -- the Windows counterpart of the O_DIRECT this same file already
+    // uses on Linux (see the POSIX branch: open(path, O_RDONLY | O_DIRECT)). The Windows port was
+    // brought up buffered, so every bundle read lands in the system file cache. On a box whose
+    // visible RAM (~15.7 GB) is comparable to the bundle (10.28 GB for SmallThinker-21B), the cache
+    // absorbs the very thing an I/O A/B is trying to measure: the POWERINFER_IOCP arms drifted
+    // upward run-over-run as the cache warmed (iocp-on 3.63 -> 4.73 -> 5.17) and never separated
+    // from the synchronous path, which is why that registry row has stayed "Direction UNRESOLVED".
+    //
+    // Requirements this satisfies, and why it is safe to add only now: NO_BUFFERING demands that the
+    // file offset, the transfer length AND the destination buffer all be sector-aligned. ExpertCache
+    // already allocates each buffer with az::aligned_alloc(io_alignment, ...), and as of the
+    // padded-stride change it also issues every read at a stride-aligned offset for a full
+    // stride-sized length. Before that change the unpadded length would have made these reads fail
+    // with ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER for any model whose matrix was not already 4096-aligned.
+    //
+    // Default OFF. This is a measurement instrument first: it must be possible to A/B it against the
+    // buffered path on the same binary, and turning it on by default would silently change the
+    // meaning of every streaming number recorded so far.
+    if (const char * nb = std::getenv("POWERINFER_NO_BUFFERING")) {
+        if (nb[0] == '1' && nb[1] == '\0') {
+            create_flags |= FILE_FLAG_NO_BUFFERING;
+        }
+    }
+
     HANDLE h = CreateFileA(path.c_str(), GENERIC_READ, FILE_SHARE_READ, nullptr,
                            OPEN_EXISTING, create_flags, nullptr);
     POWERINFER_ASSERT(h != INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE);
